From d3ede7214b7442337204fb324d61dc361a36cde6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Rota <simone.rota16@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:50:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/19] fix(EDDI): temporary duplicates of arguments are valid
 for one call

temporaryArgumentDuplication created the copy at the call site and stored it
in DuplicatedInstructionMap, so a second call in another block reused an
alloca that does not dominate it (broken module) or a stale snapshot. The
copies are now allocated in the entry block (also not to grow the stack in
loops) and removed from the map after the call. Moreover: the size of the
memcpy was an i8 (sizes >= 256 were truncated), the copy of a GEP was an alloca
with a ConstantInt of the element type as array size (invalid for non-integer
types) and null pointers were dereferenced.
The temporary copy of a constant global stored by a store instruction is
removed: it lived in the stack frame of the function, and a pointer to it
stored in a global or returned would dangle; both copies now store the
address of the constant.
